## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the KubeWize project following the latest official documentation.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**
1. `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component to root layout
   - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after children
   - Maintained existing structure and formatting

2. `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
   - Installed `@vercel/analytics` version ^2.0.1

3. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

### Implementation Details

The project uses Next.js 14 with App Router architecture, so I followed the App Router-specific instructions:
- Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`)
- Component was placed at the end of the `<body>` tag, after the children, following best practices
- Import statement uses the framework-specific path: `@vercel/analytics/next`

### Verification Completed

✅ Build successful - `npm run build` completed without errors
✅ No linting issues - `npm run lint` passed with no warnings or errors
✅ All dependencies installed correctly
✅ Lock files updated appropriately

### Next Steps for User

To enable Web Analytics in production:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to your Vercel dashboard's Analytics section
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
4. Analytics will be automatically collected once enabled in the dashboard

The Analytics component will start tracking page views and Web Vitals once the project is deployed and the feature is enabled in the Vercel dashboard.
